perf(mens): Use BF16 for activations and embeddings on CUDA
scale: ~267 lines across 2 files [L]

- `crates/vox-plugin-mens-candle-cuda/src/model.rs`:
    - Introduced `rms_norm_f32` function to ensure F32-stable RMSNorm reduction while preserving activation dtype, casting to F32 for computation and back to input dtype.
    - Modified `Qwen2Attention` to cast QKV biases to the activation dtype (BF16 on CUDA, F32 otherwise) before broadcasting, preventing mixed-dtype operations.
    - Updated `Qwen2MLP` to cast `gate_proj` and `up_proj` biases to the activation dtype.
    - Changed `Qwen2Block` to use `rms_norm_f32` for `input_layernorm` and `post_attention_layernorm`.
    - Modified `Qwen2Model` to use `rms_norm_f32` for `norm`.
    - Updated `Qwen2Model` to load `lm_head` weights in the activation dtype.
    - Adjusted `Qwen2Model` to ensure `lm_head` biases are cast to the activation dtype.
- `crates/vox-plugin-mens-candle-cuda/src/candle_qlora_train/mod.rs`:
    - Added `activation_compute_dtype` function to determine the activation dtype (BF16 on CUDA, F32 on CPU, or F32 if `VOX_MENS_ACT_F32` is set).
    - Modified embedding loading to use the determined activation compute dtype, roughly halving activation and embedding VRAM on CUDA.
    - Updated `QLoraTrainer` initialization to pass the `activation_compute_dtype` to `QLoraConfig`.

